Ladybird computes a declaration that is invalid at computed-value
time as a declaration of unset, never as the user-agent value. Blink’s
StyleCascade returns a CSSUnsetValue when a substituted value doesn’t
parse, and WebKit’s Style::Builder applies the unset value type when
the current property is invalid at computed-value time. Firefox, too,
computes such a declaration as unset rather than as the UA value.
